{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/71277-how-does-wyrd-increase","id":71277,"title":"How does \"Wyrd\" increase?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-13T07:38:07-08:00","id":71277,"title":"How does \"Wyrd\" increase?","content":"Hi, I'm reading Changeling the Lost but I didn't understand/find the mechanics to improve the Wyrd. I mean, Vampires get Blood Potency beacuse of time and diablerie.<br /> Any help? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/828-j7hunter","name":"j7hunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T08:01:25-08:00","id":71298,"title":"","content":"Well, on a mechanical level, you increase Wyrd by spending experience points. There are no system stipulations beyond that, really.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise, a changeling's Wyrd rises by indulging their fairy natures. e.g. spending time in the Hedge or Hollow, using Contracts, a diet rich in Goblin fruits, joining an Entitlement, etc etc etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:15:06-08:00","id":71504,"title":"","content":"From a narrative point of view, I think the Wyrd increases when the Changeling side of a person becomes stronger than the mortal side.<br /> <br /> The rules suggest that your mask 'reveals' more magic as your Wyrd increases. I think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:18:09-08:00","id":71562,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree with Firefly Night in that it's mostly by indulging in their fae side like what he described but another avenue is that since Wyrd is a force in the world, not just an aspect of specific Changeling, and the &quot;Wyrd Rating&quot; represents the connection to that greater power (unlike Blood Potency which is a pseudo-physical trait of that Vampire) a possible way to increase that is by obtaining &quot;blessings&quot; from the Wyrd by catching it's attention somehow; such as being particularly heroic (or villainous) since the Wyrd loves a good story, being around other high Wyrd changelings since it might &quot;rub off&quot; on them, or just randomly since it's impossible to understand the Wyrd anyways. Though it may then come to expect great things of the ones it blesses and may set up situations to make them live up to those expectations.<br /> <br /> These would be more the exceptions than the rule, but still could add some interesting plot points if the ST wants to play around with using Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2038-joshuaflcl","name":"JoshuaFLCL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2038_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:00:35-08:00","id":71640,"title":"","content":"There are also alternative rules, I can't recall whether they're in Rites of Spring or Equinox Road, where every Contract use has a chance of increasing your Wyrd rating. This indicates that just tapping into Fae magic can attune you to the Wyrd more strongly, and increase your Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:11:29-08:00","id":71652,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, any given Trait is increased by exercising that Trait. For Supernatural Tolerance stats this amounts to using and experiencing your splat's associated magic and metaphysics. Wyrd's no different, as can be determined from the writeup on page 83 of the corebook:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Lost characters begin play knowing how to tap into only a small fraction of this tremendous power. As they experiment with their new powers, however, they find their magic growing in strength, their memories of their servitude returning with greater clarity and even some of their fundamental human limits pushed aside, allowing them to develop all manner of astounding capabilities both magical and mundane. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T16:17:31-08:00","id":71692,"title":"","content":"Ok guys, I got it! I was a bit surprised because the lack of mechanincs, but that's not a problem if it's a narrative matter. <br /> <br /> A lot of thanks you all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/828-j7hunter","name":"j7hunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T07:12:28-08:00","id":73699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/71277-how-does-wyrd-increase?p=71298#post71298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fluff wise, a changeling's Wyrd rises by indulging their fairy natures. e.g. spending time in the Hedge or Hollow, using Contracts, a diet rich in Goblin fruits, joining an Entitlement, etc etc etc</div> </div> </div> </div>So...they become a bit &quot;Wyrd&quot;-er?<br /> <br /> (I'll go in the corner now.......)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}